              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Because \"Glenwood Pool\" can refer to several different well-known locations across the United States, here are details on the most prominent ones to help you find the right one:\n\n### 1. Glenwood Hot Springs Pool (Glenwood Springs, Colorado)\nThis is the most famous \"Glenwood Pool\" in the country. \n* **What it is:** Located at the historic **Glenwood Hot Springs Resort**, this is the **world's largest mineral hot springs pool**. \n* **Key Features:** It features a massive Grand Pool (kept at a comfortable 90\u00b0F/32\u00b0C), a hotter Therapy Pool (104\u00b0F/40\u00b0C), and the Sopris Splash Zone (which includes water slides and a fountain play area). \n* **Access:** Open to resort guests and the general public (day passes are available).\n\n### 2. Glenwood Pool (Silver Spring / Forest Glen, Maryland)\n* **What it is:** A private, member-supported community swim club located at 10012 Gardiner Ave, Silver Spring, MD. It has been a neighborhood fixture since 1953.\n* **Key Features:** Set back in a wooded area along a creek, it features a main pool, a swim and dive team (the Glenwood Tigers), and active community events. \n* **Access:** Membership-based. Due to its popularity, there is historically a waitlist to join.\n\n### 3. Glenwood Pool (Columbus, Ohio)\n* **What it is:** A public outdoor pool managed by the Columbus Recreation and Parks Department, located at Glenwood Park (1888 Fairmont Ave). \n* **Key Features:** After undergoing a major complete redesign and reopening, the modern facility features a 6-lane Junior Olympic lap pool, an activity pool with a zero-entry edge, a wading pool, water slides, and a diving pool with 1-meter boards.\n* **Access:** Open to the public during the summer. Admission requires a free Columbus Recreation and Parks \"Leisure Card\" plus a standard daily entry fee or season pass.\n\n### 4. Glenwood Park Pool (Atlanta, Georgia)\n* **What it is:** A private neighborhood pool located in the Glenwood Park community. \n* **Key Features:** A 6-lane, Junior Olympic-sized outdoor saline pool, an adjacent kids' splash and water play area, and a fitness center.\n* **Access:** Requires neighborhood residency or an approved outside membership.\n\n***\n\n**Which \"Glenwood Pool\" were you looking for?** Let me know if you need specific hours of operation, entry fees, membership details, or directions for any of these locations!",
